# {{PROJECT}}

An [Ohm](https://) hardware design — typed, physics-aware, compiled.

## Prerequisites

`ohm` must be on your PATH. From the Ohm source tree, `pipx install .` puts it
there globally (no venv to activate); or activate Ohm's virtualenv. Verify your
environment any time:

```sh
ohm doctor
```

## Workflow

```sh
ohm check                    # all checks, no output files (fast inner loop)
ohm build                    # netlist + KiCad project + zen + constraints -> out/
ohm explain <CODE>           # explain any diagnostic, e.g. ohm explain C001
ohm fmt {{STEM}}.ohm --write   # canonical formatting
```

`ohm.toml` lets the commands above run with no file argument from anywhere in
this project. You can always be explicit: `ohm build {{STEM}}.ohm -o out/`.

## Layout

```
{{STEM}}.ohm       the top-level design (the module `ohm build` compiles)
ohm.toml           project config (entry file, out dir, target)
lib/               your reusable component blocks — use "./lib/parts.ohm"
out/               build artifacts (git-ignored)
docs/LANGUAGE.md   the Ohm language reference for this project
AGENTS.md          contract for LLM agents authoring this design
```

## Authoring

The language is small and declarative — start with
[`docs/LANGUAGE.md`](docs/LANGUAGE.md). Working with an AI agent? Point it at
[`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) first, then let it iterate against `ohm check
--json-diagnostics`.
